# PR delivery gate (CI)

When committing, opening a PR, pushing commits meant for review, handing off,
or saying a PR task is **done**:

1. Run **CI-parity local checks** first — `npm run format:check`, `npm run lint`,
   `npm run architecture-guard`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test -- --ci` (see
   [commands.mdc](./commands.mdc)). Fix before commit.
2. Invoke the repo **`code-reviewer`** agent (`.claude/agents/code-reviewer.md`)
   on the **working diff** (before commit). Fix **all** findings before commit
   (Blocking, Should-fix, Nit — every severity), then commit → push. Only skip a
   finding with an explicit per-item human waiver in the PR body. Do not hand
   off or merge while any finding remains unfixed without that waiver.
3. After `gh pr create` / push: **watch CI** (`gh pr checks --watch` or
   equivalent) until required checks finish.
4. On failure: fix, push, re-watch. Do not hand off as complete while checks
   are red or still running.
5. Only report “done” when required CI is green (or you explicitly document an
   out-of-scope base-branch blocker).

Canonical flow: `.claude/commands/create-pr.md` (local checks + review before
commit + CI wait). `/open-pr` is an alias. Human merges — agents do not merge;
do not merge over unfixed review findings.
